<div id="aviation" v-cloak>
  <div purpose="page-container">
    <div purpose="page-content">

      <div purpose="page-hero">
        <div purpose="page-heading">
          <h4>Aviation</h4>
          <h1>Same airframe, new engine</h1>
        </div>
        <div purpose="hero-text">
          <p>Upgrade to AI-native device management to be more efficient and more secure.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="button-row">
          <a purpose="cta-button" href="/contact?talkToUs">Get a demo</a>
          <animated-arrow-button href="/fast-track">See how switching works</animated-arrow-button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="pain-banner">
        <div purpose="pain-text">
          <h2>What's holding airlines back</h2>
          <div purpose="pain-items">
            <div purpose="pain-item">
              <h5>Microsoft E3/E5 feels inescapable</h5>
              <p>Many organizations still believe you need Entra and Intune to manage Windows devices, even in regulated environments.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="pain-item">
              <h5>New devices cost more than they should</h5>
              <p>In the past, zero-touch setup often meant another license, and a USB stick for everything else.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="pain-item">
              <h5>The basics eat the budget</h5>
              <p>Patching and escalations take IT's focus, and there isn’t much left for what really matters: the employee experience.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div purpose="pain-image">
          <img alt="A passenger jet in flight against a cloudy sky" src="/images/aviation-pain-airplane-487x561@2x.jpg">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <img alt="Introducing Fleet" src="/images/endpoint-governance-introducing-fleet-193x28@2x.png">
          <h2>The new engine for airline IT</h2>
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-rows">
          <div purpose="feature-with-image">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <div purpose="teams-animation" role="img" aria-label="A Microsoft Teams chat with Fleet. An admin asks what it takes to meet CIS Level 2 on their Windows devices. Fleet reports that 2,184 of 2,350 Windows hosts pass Level 1, that Level 2 adds 38 settings, and that the biggest gaps are Credential Guard, telemetry limits, and unneeded services, then offers to propose changes to close those gaps. The admin says yes, and Fleet proposes 3 new profiles and 38 policies for their review.">
                <div purpose="teams-window" aria-hidden="true">
                  <img purpose="teams-chrome" alt="" src="/images/aviation-teams-chat-window-560x576.svg">
                  <div purpose="teams-messages">
                    <div purpose="teams-message-stack">
                      <div purpose="teams-first-message">
                        <p><strong>@Fleet</strong> what do we need for CIS level 2 on our Windows devices?</p>
                      </div>
                      <div purpose="teams-first-reply">
                        <div purpose="teams-typing">
                          <img purpose="teams-avatar" alt="" src="/images/icon-fleet-avatar-28x28.svg">
                          <div purpose="teams-typing-bubble"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
                        </div>
                        <div purpose="teams-reply">
                          <img purpose="teams-avatar" alt="" src="/images/icon-fleet-avatar-28x28.svg">
                          <div purpose="teams-reply-body">
                            <span purpose="teams-sender">Fleet</span>
                            <div purpose="teams-reply-bubble">
                              <p>2,184 of 2,350 Windows hosts pass Level 1. Level 2 adds 38 settings. The biggest gaps are Credential Guard, telemetry limits, and unneeded services.</p>
                            </div>
                            <div purpose="teams-follow-up">
                              <div purpose="teams-reply-bubble">
                                <p>Want me to propose changes that close those gaps?</p>
                              </div>
                            </div>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div purpose="teams-second-message">
                        <p>Yes</p>
                      </div>
                      <div purpose="teams-second-reply">
                        <div purpose="teams-typing">
                          <img purpose="teams-avatar" alt="" src="/images/icon-fleet-avatar-28x28.svg">
                          <div purpose="teams-typing-bubble"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
                        </div>
                        <div purpose="teams-reply">
                          <img purpose="teams-avatar" alt="" src="/images/icon-fleet-avatar-28x28.svg">
                          <div purpose="teams-reply-body">
                            <span purpose="teams-sender">Fleet</span>
                            <div purpose="teams-reply-bubble">
                              <p>Done. I’ve proposed 3 new profiles and 38 policies <span purpose="teams-link">for your review</span>.</p>
                            </div>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div purpose="feature-text">
              <h3>Deliver entire IT projects in minutes, not&nbsp;weeks</h3>
              <p>Ask Fleet in plain language for what you need, and fix it right&nbsp;away.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-with-image" class="reverse">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="A new computer installing apps automatically during setup" src="/images/aviation-zero-touch-504x378@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="feature-text">
              <h3>Zero-touch setup, no Autopilot required</h3>
              <p>Use Autopilot and Entra if you have them, but you don’t need them. Zero touch works on Apple, Windows, and Linux, and already runs on thousands of Windows devices in production.</p>
              <a purpose="video-button" @click="clickOpenVideoModal('zero-touch-setup')"><img alt="Play" src="/images/icon-play-video-32x32@2x.png">See how it works</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-with-image">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Patch options in Fleet and the notification employees see before apps update" src="/images/aviation-patch-notification-504x378@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="feature-text">
              <h3>Get time back</h3>
              <p>When the basics run themselves, IT has time for what really matters: the productivity of the people who use the devices.</p>
              <div purpose="stats">
                <div purpose="stat">
                  <h3>50–80%</h3>
                  <p>Less time on maintenance, as reported by Fleet customers.</p>
                </div>
                <div purpose="stat">
                  <h3>10mins</h3>
                  <p>Average new hire time to productivity.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="quote-section">
        <div purpose="quote-author-image">
          <img alt="Swan avatar" src="/images/aviation-quote-swan-64x64@2x.png">
        </div>
        <p purpose="quote-text">“Like the A320 with its new engine option, we're swapping the engines before we scale up Macs: more efficient, cheaper, and more secure. Fleet is the new engine.”</p>
        <div purpose="name-and-title">
          <p purpose="author-name">Senior IT Security Architect</p>
          <p purpose="author-title">Major European airline</p>
        </div>
      </div>

